  "id": "preparation",
  "term": "preparation",
  "definition": "In cognition, preparation can refer to a readiness state in which expecting a stimulus sharpens attention and speeds simple responses, as shown in the preparation effect. This benefit appears strongest when timing or occurrence is highly certain, remains stable over time, and depends on the demands of the response task.",
